 "id": "01a0fc69-3502-78b2-a75e-0bc54371c3f9",
 "content": "scripts/export.py produces the monthly invoice report that Finance imports into their accounting tool at the start of each month. It runs from the ops cron on the 2nd at 06:00 UTC and writes one file per environment to EXPORT_BUCKET under `exports/<YYYY-MM>/invoices.csv`. Finance reconciles the totals against the ledger, so every finalized invoice of the month must appear exactly once, including zero-amount ones; drafts are excluded. Columns, in order: invoice id, customer id, subtotal, tax, total, finalized date. Amounts are integer cents with no currency symbol. Format (since Finance moved to a new accounting tool in late September 2026): plain comma-separated (`,`) CSV, dates in ISO format `YYYY-MM-DD`, UTF-8 without a BOM. The previous tool's German-locale format (semicolon delimiter, `DD.MM.YYYY` dates) is no longer used.",
 "details": "Format changed 2026-10-02 per user: \"Finance moved to a new accounting tool last week: it wants plain comma-separated files with ISO dates (YYYY-MM-DD) now.\""
}
